Android Studio Badge Unit Analysis
📘 Overview
This unit covers three pathways that build your foundation in Android development using Kotlin and Jetpack Compose:

Kotlin Fundamentals – Learn variables, functions, classes, and lambdas.

Add a Button to an App – Understand how to handle user interactions and button clicks.

Interacting with UI and State – Manage dynamic data and user input to create responsive apps.

💡 Kotlin Basics
In this unit, Kotlin is introduced as a modern, concise, and safe programming language for Android.
You learn:

Declaring variables (val, var)

Writing functions and using parameters

Performing basic math operations

Using string templates ("Hello, $name")

Understanding object-oriented concepts and lambdas

These fundamentals prepare you to move from console programs to Android apps.

🎨 Birthday Card App (Android Studio)
As part of the learning journey, you create a Birthday Card app using Jetpack Compose.
This project demonstrates:

How to design a simple UI with Text, Image, and Button components

How to use @Composable functions

How to preview layouts in Android Studio

How to respond to user input and manage state
